// ==WindhawkMod==
// @id              start-orb
// @name            Start Orb
// @description     Turns the Windows 11 Start button into an animated orb: pick a built-in orb from a menu, or use your own picture
// @version         1.0.0
// @author          frozt
// @github          https://github.com/Frozt-src
// @include         explorer.exe
// @architecture    x86-64
// @compilerOptions -lole32 -loleaut32 -lruntimeobject
// ==/WindhawkMod==

// ==WindhawkModReadme==
/*
# Start Orb

Puts an animated orb on the Windows 11 Start button.

![The five built-in orbs](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Frozt-src/windhawk-mods/start-orb-assets/start-orb-preview.gif)

1. Pick an orb.
2. Pick a size.
3. Click "Save settings".

That is all. The orb appears straight away.

## Using your own picture

Set "Orb" to "Custom". In File Explorer, right-click your picture, choose "Copy as path", and paste
it into "Picture" under "Customize". A web address (`https://...`) works too. PNG, JPG and GIF are
supported, and an animated GIF plays. If a picture can't be loaded, the normal Windows logo stays.

Two optional extras: a different picture while the pointer is on Start, and another while you click.

## Making your own animated orb

A GIF plays as it is, but it has no soft edges, so it only looks right on the bar colour it was made
for. Animated PNG and WebP files show only their first frame. For a smooth animated orb with soft
edges, use a sprite sheet: one PNG with every frame side by side in a single row. Type the number of
frames into "Animation frames" and the mod plays them.

It works alongside other taskbar mods, including Windows 11 Taskbar Styler: it does not use the
XAML diagnostics channel that only one mod can hold. If a Styler theme also restyles the Start
button, remove that part of the theme so the two do not draw over each other.

The orb appears as soon as the mod is enabled. To manage that, the mod makes each taskbar lay itself
out once, by narrowing its content by one pixel for a moment.
*/
// ==/WindhawkModReadme==

// ==WindhawkModSettings==
/*
- orb: obsidian
  $name: Orb
  $description: The orb on your Start button.
  $options:
  - obsidian: Obsidian (dark glass)
  - green: Green (glowing energy)
  - wisp: Wisp (white smoke)
  - ember: Ember (molten glass)
  - emberglow: Ember Glow (light only)
  - custom: Custom
- size: medium
  $name: Size
  $description: How big the orb is. It shrinks by itself on a small taskbar.
  $options:
  - small: Small
  - medium: Medium
  - large: Large
- hideOriginal: true
  $name: Hide the Windows logo
  $description: Turn this off to keep the normal Start icon showing behind the orb.
- myPicture:
  - image: ""
    $name: Picture
    $description: >-
      In File Explorer, right-click your picture, choose "Copy as path" and paste it here. PNG, JPG
      or GIF. A web address works too.
  - hoverImage: ""
    $name: Picture while pointing at Start
    $description: Optional. Leave empty to keep the same picture.
  - pressedImage: ""
    $name: Picture while clicking Start
    $description: Optional. Leave empty to keep the same picture.
  - frames: 1
    $name: Animation frames
    $description: >-
      Leave at 1 for a normal picture or a GIF. Only change it for a sprite sheet (one PNG with
      every frame side by side in a row): type how many frames it has.
  - frameTime: 40
    $name: Animation speed
    $description: Milliseconds per frame, for a sprite sheet. Smaller is faster. 40 is smooth.
  $name: Customize
  $description: Only used when "Orb" is set to "Custom". Skip it if you picked a built-in orb.
*/
// ==/WindhawkModSettings==

